{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"Explicit q-AND amplitudes at the substrate value $q_0$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-toffoli-transfer-matrix","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-local-substrate-q"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-toffoli-transfer-matrix","text":"toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation\"></a><p><strong>Explicit values at the local substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = q_0 \\approx 1.110</code>, with Markov parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code>:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Entry</th>\n<th>Symbolic</th>\n<th align=\"center\">Numerical</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{6,6}</code> (no flip, even)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dfrac{(q^4+1)(q^4+q^2+2)}{4q(q^2+1)^2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.5407</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{7,7}</code> (no flip, odd)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dfrac{q^3(q^4+1)}{(q^2+1)^2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.6912</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{7,6}</code> (flip)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-\\dfrac{(q-1)(q+1)(q^6+q^4+2q^2+1)}{2q(q^2+1)^2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.1438</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{6,7}</code> (reverse flip)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dfrac{(q-1)(q+1)(2q^6+q^4+q^2+1)}{2q(q^2+1)^2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.1572</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0 \\approx 1.110</code>, both diagonal channels are strictly positive whereas the forward target-flip amplitude <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_{7,6}(q_0) \\approx -0.1438</code> is negative. Moreover, the flip channel is <strong>not</strong> antisymmetric: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|P_{6,7}(q_0)| \\approx 0.1572 \\neq |P_{7,6}(q_0)| \\approx 0.1438</code>, because each entry is evaluated against its own parent input column.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"22.6.2","page":"b/rem-toffoli-transfer-matrix-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":51,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":37,"unknown":0,"stale":17},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
